{
  "title": "Dua for fulfillment of wishes",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "اَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ السَّمٰوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَ مَا بَيْنَهُنَّ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBAS SAMAAWAATIS SAB-E WA MAA BAYNAHUNNA\nO Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what is between them,\nوَ رَبَّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA RABBAL ARSHIL AZEEM\nand Lord of the Mighty Throne,\nوَ رَبَّ جَبْرَئِيْلَ وَ مِيْكَاۤئِيْلَ وَ اِسْرَافِيْلَ\nWA RABBA JABRA-EELA WA MEEKAA-EELA WA ISRAAFEEL\nand Lord of Jibra'il, Mika'il, and Israfil,\nوَ رَبَّ الْقُرْاٰنِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA RABBAL QUR-AANIL AZEEM\nand Lord of the Great Qur'an,\nوَ رَبَّ مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nWA RABBA MOHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nand Lord of Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets,\nاِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِالَّذِيْ تَقُوْمُ بِهِ السَّمَاۤءُ وَ بِهِ تَقُوْمُ الْاَرْضُ\nINNEE AS-ALOKA BILLAZEE TAQOOMO BEHIS SAMAA-O WA BEHI TAQOOMUL ARZO\nverily I ask You by that through which the sky stands and through which the earth stands,\nوَ بِهِ تُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ الْجَمْعِ وَ بِهِ تَجْمَعُ بَيْنَ الْمُتَفَرِّقِ\nWA BEHI TUFARRIQO BAYNAL JAM-E WA BEHI TAJMA-O BAYNAL MUTAFARRIQ\nand through which You separate what is joined and join what is separated,\nوَ بِهِ تَرْزُقُ الْاَحْيَاۤءَ\nWA BEHI TARZUQUL AHYAA-A\nand through which You give sustenance to the living,\nوَ بِهِ اَحْصَيْتَ عَدَدَ الرِّمَالِ وَ وَزْنَ الْجِبَالِ وَ كَيْلَ الْبُحُوْرِ\nWA BEHI AHSAYTA ADADAR REMAALE WA WAZNAL JEBAALE WA KAYLAL BUHOOR\nand through which You have counted the number of the sands, the weight of the mountains, and the measure of the seas.\n\nHaving said this, invoke Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household and submit your request, preferably insistently.",
  "merits": "Reported to be the supplication of insistence. Shaykh al-Tusi, in Misbah al-Mutahajjid, mentions it to be said immediately after the fourth unit of the Night Prayer; al-Majlisi (compiler of Bihar al-Anwar) reported Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) recommending it in the single-unit Witr Prayer."
